,245,498) ($1,999,714) Free cash flow $10,921,066 $2,496,026 About Meridian Holdings Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN) is a sports betting and gaming group headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada. The Company operates online and retail sports betting and casino gaming in 19 jurisdictions across Europe, Africa and Central and South America. Its betting and casino brands include Meridianbet, founded in Serbia in 2001 and active in 18 jurisdictions, and MexPlay in Mexico. RKings runs pay-to-enter prize competitions in the United Kingdom, and Classics for a Cause runs trade promotions in Australia. The Company’s B2B businesses include Expanse Studios, which develops and licenses casino games, and GMAG, which resells third-party gaming content, mainly in Asia-Pacific. For more information, visit www.meridian-holdings.com . Non-GAAP Financial Measures EBITDA, Adjusted EBITDA, Net Debt, Net Debt Leverage Ratio and Free Cash Flow are non-Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) financial measures presented as supplemental indicators of the Company’s performance and capital structure. EBITDA represents net income (loss) before interest expense, interest income, income taxes, and depreciation and amortization. Adjusted EBITDA represents EBITDA further adjusted to exclude stock-based compensation expense, unrealized foreign exchange gains or losses, severance costs related to the termination of executive officers and directors, impairment losses on goodwill and other intangible assets, and restructuring costs, which include charges or expenses attributable to acquisition-related costs. Beginning in the first quarter of 2026, the Company changed its definition of Adjusted EBITDA to exclude unrealized foreign exchange gains and losses. Management believes this adjustment facilitates period-to-period comparisons of operating performance because these non-cash gains and losses primarily reflect fluctuations in foreign currency exchange rates. The Company recast the prior-period Adjusted EBITDA amounts presented below to conform to the current definition. Adjusted EBITDA for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025 was $4.8 million and $14.0 million, respectively, after excluding unrealized foreign exchange gains of $0.9 million and $0.8 million, respectively. The Company previously reported Adjusted EBITDA of $5.7 million and $14.8 million for those periods, respectively. Net Debt is defined as total debt, less cash and cash equivalents. Net Debt Leverage Ratio is defined as Net Debt at the balance sheet date divided by annualized Adjusted EBITDA for the period then ended, calculated for the third quarter of 2026 as Adjusted EBITDA for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, multiplied by four-thirds. Free Cash Flow is defined as net cash provided by operating activities less cash paid for intangible assets, cash paid for property, plant and equipment, and repayment of leases. Free Cash Flow does not represent cash available for discretionary spending, because it does not deduct required debt repayments. We present EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA because we believe these measures provide investors with additional insight into our core operating performance by excluding the effects of financing costs, income taxes, depreciation and amortization, and, in the case of Adjusted EBITDA, certain non-cash and other specified items. We present Net Debt and the Net Debt Leverage Ratio to provide investors with a better understanding of our indebtedness, net of cash and cash equivalents, and our leverage relative to earnings. We present Free Cash Flow to provide insight into the cash generated from operating activities after investments in intangible assets and property, plant and equipment, and lease payments. We believe these non-GAAP financial measures, when considered together with our GAAP financial results, provide useful supplemental information for evaluating our operating performance, cash generation, liquidity and financial position. These measures are non-GAAP measures, are unaudited, and have inherent limitations as analytical tools. These measures should not be considered in isolation, or as substitutes for analysis of the Company’s results as reported under GAAP. Some of these limitations include: they do not reflect cash expenditures or future capital requirements; they do not reflect working capital requirements or contractual commitments; they do not reflect significant interest expense, principal, or income tax payments; although depreciation and amortization are non-cash charges, the assets being depreciated or amortized may require replacement in the future; and other companies may calculate these measures differently, limiting comparability. The Company’s presentation of these measures should not be construed as implying that future results will be unaffected by unusual or non-recurring items. For additional information regarding these non-GAAP financial measures, please refer to the sections titled “Reconciliation of U.S. GAAP Net Income (Loss) to EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA (Unaudited)” and “Reconciliation of Net Debt and Leverage Calculation (Unaudited)”, included at the end of this release. Free Cash Flow is reconciled to net cash provided by operating activities in the table “Reconciliation of Net Cash Provided by Operating Activities to Free Cash Flow (Unaudited)”, also at the end of this release. The Company does not provide a reconciliation of forward-looking Adjusted EBITDA to the most directly comparable GAAP financial measure because it is unable to do so without unreasonable effort due to the inherent uncertainty in forecasting certain items, including, but not limited to, stock-based compensation, transaction-related expenses, and other non-recurring or non-cash items; accordingly, a reconciliation is not available without unreasonable effort, and the unavailable information could have a material impact on the Company’s future GAAP financial results. Forward-Looking S