etta, Malta and Las Vegas, NV  ·  October 13, 2026 Launch activates the studio’s software provider license and marks its first revenue-generating deployment in the Swedish market Expanse Studios (“Expanse”), the B2B game development division of Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN) (“Meridian” or the “Company”), today announced that its subsidiary and B2B game development division Expanse Studios (“Expanse”) has gone live with a Swedish Gambling Authority-licensed operator in Sweden. The launch is the studio’s first live operator deployment in the Swedish market and the first commercial activation of the software provider license awarded to Expanse by the Swedish Gambling Authority (Spelinspektionen) in December 2025, valid through December 2030. Sweden operates one of Europe’s most tightly regulated online gaming markets. Every operator must hold a Spelinspektionen license, and player activity is concentrated heavily on licensed platforms, making each certified supplier relationship a route to regulated, channelized demand rather than gray-market volume. Content providers working with licensed Swedish operators ensures technical and compliance standing in addition to commercial reach. “A license is the permission to compete. Going live is the proof that our content clears the bar. Sweden holds one of the most demanding regulatory standards in Europe. Launching with a licensed operator there confirms that our content and compliance meet that standard in practice, not just on paper.” Damjan Stamenkovic  · Chief Executive Officer, Expanse Studios The Swedish launch adds a mature Western European market to Expanse Studios’ footprint. The studio holds content certifications across 14 regulated markets in Europe, Latin America and Africa, including Sweden, Malta, Portugal, Croatia, Romania, Estonia, Latvia, Slovenia, Brazil and Colombia. Expanse distributes a portfolio of nearly 100 proprietary titles to more than 1,800 online casino brands worldwide. Expanding certified, revenue-generating distribution across regulated markets supports Meridian Holdings’ strategy of growing B2B revenue alongside its B2C operations. About Expanse Studios Expanse Studios, part of Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN), is a B2B iGaming content provider specializing in slots, crash games, turn-based strategies and card games. The studio distributes a portfolio of nearly 100 proprietary titles to operators across Europe, Latin America and North America, and holds content certifications across 14 regulated markets in Europe, Latin America and Africa. Learn more at expanse.studio . About Meridian Holdings Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN), headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada, is a B2B and B2C gaming technology group operating across over 25 international regulated markets. The Company’s B2C division is led by Meridianbet Group, an online sports betting and gaming operator founded in 2001 and licensed across Europe, Africa and South America. The Company’s B2B division, comprising game developer Expanse Studios and iGaming platform GMAG, develops, licenses and distributes proprietary gaming platforms and content to a global client base. For more information, visit www.meridian-holdings.com or email ir@meridian-holdings.com . Investor & Media Contact Investors & Press: Meridian: ir@meridian-holdings.com ICR: meridian@icrinc.com ]]> https://meridian-holdings.com/news/meridian-holdings-expanse-studios-now-live-in-sweden/feed/ 0 Meridian Holdings Provides Update on Brazilian Provisional Measure, Confirms Expected Immaterial Exposure https://meridian-holdings.com/news/meridian-holdings-provides-update-on-brazilian-provisional-measure-confirms-expected-immaterial-exposure/ https://meridian-holdings.com/news/meridian-holdings-provides-update-on-brazilian-provisional-measure-confirms-expected-immaterial-exposure/#respond Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:47:00 +0000 https://meridian-holdings.com/?p=8311 Las Vegas, NV  ·  September 29, 2026  · NewMediaWire Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN) (the “Company” or “Meridian Holdings”), an international developer, licensor, and operator of online gaming and e-commerce platforms, today provided the below update relating to the Provisional Measure signed by the President of Brazil on September 25, 2026, which prohibits the operation, intermediation and advertising of online betting and online casino services in Brazil and requires that funds be returned to bettors. The measure is provisional and is expected to be subject to approval by the Brazilian Congress (within 120 days of adoption) to remain in effect. Brazil represents an immaterial share of Meridian Holdings’ Group revenue. The Company’s Meridianbet brand operates in Brazil through its subsidiary Meridian Gaming Brasil SPE Ltda, which holds authorisation SPA/MF n° 0086/2024, granted by Portaria SPA/MF n° 526 of March 14, 2025, for the operation of fixed-odds sports betting and online gaming. The Company has been, and continues to be, fully compliant with the Provisional Measure and all applicable regulatory requirements in Brazil. The Company entered the Brazilian market on a conservative basis and did not commit large-scale marketing expenditure in advance of licensing. Its exposure to the measure is limited as a result. The Company’s authorization in Brazil was granted until December 31, 2029. The Company is reviewing the Provisional Measure and its implications with its Brazilian and United States legal advisers. Under Brazilian law, a Provisional Measure takes effect on publication in the Diario Oficial da Uniao and has immediate force of law. It is valid for 60 days and may be extended once for a further 60 days. The Brazilian Congress must approve it within that period, failing which it ceases to have effect. About Meridian Holdings Meridian Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: MRDN), headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada, is a B2B and B2C gaming technology group operating across over 25 international regulated markets. The Company’s B2C divisio